# Finders

## Framework semantics

Custom finders encapsulate reusable query modifications and remain composable with other conditions.

## Required behavior

- Prefer finders over copying filter logic into controllers.
- Keep finders composable; avoid surprising hard limits unless documented.
- Use `aliasField()` when ambiguity is possible.

## Anti-patterns

- Duplicate finders / duplicate query semantics
- Non-composable finders that break further where/contain

## Review checklist

- [ ] Finder is reusable and tested
- [ ] Does not introduce N+1 by default